{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe day was warm, the dust thick. We drove with Raumer to Saint-Denis; the cathedral still hung in black for a recent funeral. A strange, heavy silence there. We pressed on to Montmorency. I took a donkey to the Hermitage, Rousseau’s old spot. The animal was stubborn, but the view from the heights was grand—Paris and Montmartre stretching out below like a map.\n\nRaumer is talkative, full of French politics, but he listens well when I speak. We dined at a small inn; the wine was decent, the bread heavy. I paid five francs for the ride and supper. My legs ache, but the mind is clear.\n\nYou asked of the books I sent. They should be there by next week. Tell Karl his father thinks him too hasty in his essays on ethics; let him read more history. I miss your quiet room and the sound of the children.\n\nI am tired. Sleep well.\n\nYour G.W.F.H."}}],"created":1795219403,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":218,"prompt_tokens":1127,"total_tokens":1345,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-ScRb7x1HrFS5x1ml3YuGr6YbPlOFSI3v","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1127,"prompt_ms":1080.422,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9586708074534162,"prompt_per_second":1043.1109325800473,"predicted_n":218,"predicted_ms":5150.212,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.733695852534563,"predicted_per_second":42.134187874207896}}